/composer.phar

# HDP: re-allow the two composer files this fork deliberately commits.
#
# Upstream MediaWiki ignores composer.lock and composer.local.json because MW
# core does not ship them. HDP does — and both are load-bearing:
#
#   composer.lock        setup.sh strips hallowelt/chatbot and
#                        mediawiki/page-header from it at install time, and
#                        composer install resolves 353 packages from it.
#   composer.local.json  declares the "pre-autoload-dump" hook that runs all
#                        eight scripts in _bluespice/pre-autoload-dump.d/,
#                        including the one applying the 17 .diff patches.
#
# Both were tracked while still matching the ignore rules above, which is the
# failure mode docs/QA-REPORT.md Bug 2 describes: the file is present on the
# maintainer's disk, so nothing looks wrong, but `git add -A` silently refuses
# to re-add it if it is ever removed. That is how the Vector HookRunner.php
# fix was lost. Negating the rules makes the intent explicit and keeps the
# files re-addable.
!/composer.lock
!/composer.local.json

